    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67181" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετοικ-ία</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>change of abode, removal,
				migration</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.2
			</span></i> (pl.); of the Jewish <i>captivity</i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Je.</u>
				20.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>settlement</i> or <i>residence in a foreign city</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				1018
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				850c
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ἡ ἄνω</span>
			<i>sojourn</i> in the upper world, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				890
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>status and rights of a</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέτοικος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				6.49
			</span></i>.</div>
